{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage"]}],"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Choosing a storage","modules":[{"name":"FirebladeECS"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS"]]},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Benchmarks","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials"}],"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick the sparse-set or the archetype storage for a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and know what changes."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps its entities and components in one of two storages, chosen when it is created:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let nexus = Nexus()                       \/\/ the default, same as Nexus(storage: .archetype)","let churning = Nexus(storage: .sparseSet) \/\/ for heavy add\/remove churn"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both storages offer the same API with the same observable behavior: generational entity identifiers, events, the structural lock and its traps, families, "},{"code":"forEach(reading:writing:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", spans, snapshots, cloning and the entity state machine. Every test of the package runs against both. What differs is where the components live in memory, and with it what is cheap."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/default","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", so "},{"code":"Nexus()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" uses it. Choose "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" explicitly for workloads dominated by heavy component add and remove churn (see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#Which-storage-to-pick","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). There is no storage protocol: the set of storages is closed, and a nexus switches on its storage once per call, so each storage compiles to concrete code."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"The sparse-set storage","anchor":"The-sparse-set-storage","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps one dense array per component type, a paged sparse index per type that maps an entity to its slot in that array, and a bitset of component types per entity. Adding or removing a component touches the data of that one type only, and no other component moves. Looking up one component is a sparse index read plus an array read."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterating a family is the weak spot: the members of a family are stored in each component array in the order the components were added, so every extra component type costs a lookup per member, and the reads are scattered once the arrays were shuffled by churn."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"The archetype storage","anchor":"The-archetype-storage","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" follows the design of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/www.flecs.dev\/flecs\/md_docs_2Queries.html","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":": entities with exactly the same component types live in one table, with a column (an array) per component type. An index maps every entity to its table and row. Tables are created when a component set appears first, and adding or removing one component type moves the entity’s row to another table along a cached edge of the table graph."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Iterating a family visits the tables that match it, and walks their columns linearly: no lookup per member and a sequential read per component. The list of matching tables is cached per family, which the nexus lists when the family is created and extends when a new table appears. A table that became empty stays alive, along with its columns and its entry in the cached lists, where an iteration skips it. Cleaning the nexus with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/clear()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" drops all tables.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In flecs this is the default, and sparse components are the opt-in trait (","type":"text"},{"code":"Sparse","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"): “Sparse components are stored outside of tables, which means they do not have to be moved”, trading query speed for component add and remove speed (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/SanderMertens\/flecs\/blob\/master\/docs\/ComponentTraits.md","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"). Fireblade 1.x was the reverse, a sparse set per component type; the two storages make that a choice per nexus instead of per component.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"What the numbers say","anchor":"What-the-numbers-say","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Measured with 10 000 entities, release build, Apple silicon, wall clock p50 per pass (","type":"text"},{"code":"make benchmark","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", see ","type":"text"},{"code":"Benchmarks\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"):","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","alignments":["left","right","right"],"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Case"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sparse set"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Archetype"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"11 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2.5 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, B)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"18 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4.3 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, B, C, D)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"31 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"7.7 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, writing: B)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"17 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4.4 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, B, writing: C)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"23 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"6.1 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"2 reads, 10% of the entities match","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"3.6 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1.3 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"2 reads, 100 000 entities with shuffled storage order","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"227 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"27 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 reads, 1 024 different component sets"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"18 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"11 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Parameter pack, 5 reads and 2 writes"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 200 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1 800 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"type":"text","text":" over a family, 2 components"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"455 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"455 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Random "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"entity.get"},{"type":"text","text":" of one component, 10 000 lookups"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"334 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"345 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add a component to each entity and remove it again, 10 000 entities"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 180 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4 900 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create and destroy 1 000 entities with 7 components"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1 730 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 510 μs"}]}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Fireblade 1.x needed 480 μs for the plain iteration of one component and 1 220 μs for two ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IterOnlyOneComponent"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IterOnlyTwoComponents"},{"type":"text","text":"). Both storages iterate without any allocation."}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Iterating with ","type":"text"},{"code":"forEach(reading:writing:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is 1.6 to 8 times faster on the archetype storage: about 4 times in the plain case, 8 times when the sparse-set arrays are shuffled against each other, and least when the entities are spread over many small tables.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Changing the component set of an entity costs about twice as much on the archetype storage: the whole row moves. An entity that changes its component set less than once in a few frames is far ahead on iteration; a world that toggles a component on most entities every frame is better off with the sparse set.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Plain ","type":"text"},{"code":"for","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" iteration and random access cost the same on both: they look every component up per entity.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Entity creation and destruction are a bit slower on the archetype storage, because the row of every component moves with the entity.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Which storage to pick","anchor":"Which-storage-to-pick","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default is the archetype storage: it iterates faster (see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say"},{"type":"text","text":"), and iteration is what most worlds spend their time on."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The trade-off: the archetype storage buys iteration speed with the cost of moving a row whenever the component set of an entity changes. Prefer "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet"},{"type":"text","text":" when the workload is dominated by heavy add and remove churn, for example toggling a component on most entities every frame. This matches flecs, where sparse components are the opt-in trait for components that are added and removed often."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Differences you can observe","anchor":"Differences-you-can-observe","level":3},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iteration order."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The sparse-set storage visits the members of a family in the order of the family’s member list, the archetype storage table by table and row by row, and rows move when entities change tables. Neither order is a contract; use ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Entity\/identifier","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" or your own key if you need one.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Single-type spans."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(reading:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(writing:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" view one contiguous array. On the archetype storage a type is stored in one column per table, so if entities with different component sets have the type, the span views a temporary copy made table by table (and the writing variant stores it back when the closure returns, also when it throws). That costs one allocation and a copy per call, and nothing can observe the difference while the closure runs, because the type is locked.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Family spans."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Family\/forEachComponentSpan(reading:writing:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" passes one batch per matching table on the archetype storage, however the nexus was used before; the sparse-set storage passes shorter batches after churn. Both visit every member exactly once, and the closure must be correct for any batch size.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents"},{"type":"text","text":" for the spans."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS":{"title":"Getting started with Fireblade ECS","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn the API and key types Fireblade provides to compose your game or app logic."}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/gettingstartedwithfirebladeecs","role":"article"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/StorageKind/default":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/default","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The storage "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/init(storage:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" uses by default: "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol","title":"default","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"`default`","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS5NexusC","text":"Nexus","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS5NexusC11StorageKindO","text":"StorageKind","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/storagekind\/default"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/StorageKind/sparseSet":{"title":"Nexus.StorageKind.sparseSet","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"sparseSet"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One dense array per component type, a paged sparse index per type, a bitset per entity."}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/storagekind\/sparseset","role":"symbol"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ReactingToNexusEvents":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Observe structural changes and, on request, changes of component values."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","role":"article","title":"Reacting to Nexus events","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/reactingtonexusevents"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Benchmarks":{"title":"Benchmarks","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Benchmarks","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"See how FirebladeECS revisions compare on a shared workload suite, and run the comparison yourself."}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/benchmarks","role":"article"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/init(storage:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/init(storage:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Initializes a new Nexus."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/init(storage:)","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"storage","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS5NexusC","text":"Nexus","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS5NexusC11StorageKindO","text":"StorageKind","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"init(storage:)"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say","title":"What the numbers say","type":"topic","kind":"section","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage#What-the-numbers-say","abstract":[]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/clear()":{"title":"clear()","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/clear()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"clear"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Clears all data from the Nexus."}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/clear()","role":"symbol"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEvent":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A marker protocol for all Nexus events.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","role":"symbol","title":"NexusEvent","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NexusEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NexusEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexusevent"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/componentSpan(writing:_:)":{"title":"componentSpan(writing:_:)","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(writing:_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"componentSpan"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Result"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"writing"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":".Type, ("},{"kind":"keyword","text":"inout"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s11MutableSpanV","text":"MutableSpan"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":">) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Result"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"rethrows"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Result"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Gives "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" write access to all components of a type as one contiguous "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MutableSpan"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/componentspan(writing:_:)","role":"symbol"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A lightweight, fast and easy to use Entity-Component System in Swift."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS","role":"collection","title":"FirebladeECS","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/componentSpan(reading:_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/componentspan(reading:_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Gives "},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" read access to all components of a type as one contiguous "},{"code":"Span","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(reading:_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"componentSpan"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Result"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"reading"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":".Type, ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4SpanV","text":"Sp